# vdbvisualize

- Label: VDB Visualize
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 4
- Parameters: 71 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/vdbvisualize.html
- Summary (EN): Builds a Geometry output that displays several VDBs together as one coloured volume. It works like the Volume Visualization SOP, usable inside COPs without switching context.
- Résumé (FR) : Assemble plusieurs VDB (densité, couleur, émission, couleur d'émission) en un volume coloré affichable directement dans un réseau COP.

- Inputs meaning: ["density: Float VDB giving the fog density", "Cd: Float or Vector VDB giving the colour of each voxel", "emit: Float VDB giving the magnitude of self-emission", "emitcd: Float or Vector VDB giving the emission colour"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: the VDB type the source accepts", "Density Scale: fixed multiplier controlling opacity; Density Ramp remaps the density colour", "Diffuse Color: Input Range remaps the input colour to 0-1; Mode sets how the ramp applies; Diffuse Ramp maps to the final colour", "Emission: Emission Scale sets glow intensity; Input Range, Mode and Emission Ramp shape the emission amount", "Emission Color: Input Range, Mode and Emission Color Ramp shape the emission colour", "Shadows: Shadow Scale adds density for light-driven shadowing; Set Ambient Colors enables Exposed Color and Occluded Color; Ambient Shadow Scale sets self-shadow intensity from ambient lights; Shadow Color tints shadows"]

- Caveats: ["Use no ramp when unbounded values are needed, such as light-field colours or emission", "At a larger scene scale, a smaller Density Scale may be needed", "The page states that turning off a checkbox does not disable ambient shadowing; without an Ambient Shadow Scale, the Ambient Occlusion setting in Display Options controls default self-shadowing"]

